statement:
Let $R\to S\to B$ be homomorphisms of commutative rings, $I\subseteq B$ an ideal, $q:B\to C=B/I$ the quotient map, so that $C$ is an $S$-algebra and an $R$-algebra through $B$. For a ring map $X\to Y$ let $X[Y]$ be the polynomial ring over $X$ in the variables $[y]$, $y\in Y$ [def-weil-pbc-mv-polynomial-ring], $\gamma_{Y/X}:X[Y]\to Y$, $[y]\mapsto y$, the canonical presentation with kernel $I_{Y/X}$, and $H_1(L_{Y/X})\subseteq I_{Y/X}/I_{Y/X}^2$ the first homology of its naive cotangent complex [def-weil-pbc-smooth-ring-map]; let $\Omega$, $\mathrm d$ be as in [def-weil-pbc-kahler-differentials]. Let
(a) $\iota:H_1(L_{C/S})\to H_1(L_{C/B})$ be the map induced by the morphism of presentations $\lambda:S[C]\to B[C]$ (coefficients through $S\to B$, $[c]\mapsto[c]$) over the square $S\to B$, $\mathrm{id}_C$ [lem-weil-pbc-nl-presentation-h1-functoriality];
(b) $\theta:H_1(L_{C/B})\xrightarrow{\sim}I/I^2$ the isomorphism of [lem-weil-pbc-jacobi-zariski-surjection-h1] for the surjection $q:B\to C$;
(c) $\partial_S:H_1(L_{C/S})\to C\otimes_S\Omega_{S/R}$ the connecting map of the Jacobi-Zariski sequence of $R\to S\to C$ [lem-weil-pbc-jacobi-zariski-homology-sequence], which by that node is the map $g\bmod I_{C/S}^2\mapsto\sum_\alpha\gamma_{C/S}([c]^\alpha)\otimes\mathrm ds_\alpha$, where $g=\sum_\alpha s_\alpha[c]^\alpha\in I_{C/S}$ is written in the monomials $[c]^\alpha$ of $S[C]$ with coefficients $s_\alpha\in S$ ("differentiate the coefficients"); likewise $\partial_B:H_1(L_{C/B})\to C\otimes_B\Omega_{B/R}$ for $S=B$;
(d) $c:C\otimes_S\Omega_{S/R}\to C\otimes_B\Omega_{B/R}$, $x\otimes\mathrm ds\mapsto x\otimes\mathrm d(s\cdot1_B)$, and $\delta:I/I^2\to C\otimes_B\Omega_{B/R}$, $f\bmod I^2\mapsto1\otimes\mathrm df$.
Then $\partial_S$, $\partial_B$, $c$ and $\delta$ are well defined and $C$-linear, and $$\delta\circ\theta\circ\iota=c\circ\partial_S .$$ In particular (case $S=B$, where $\iota$ and $c$ are identities) $\delta\circ\theta=\partial_B$.
